   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello there,</div><div><br></div><div>I am a newbie for ggplot2.</div><div>I would like to change axis ticks like the attached jpg (GraphDesired.jpg).</div><div>Usually the exponent label is attached to the axis itself (see GraphUndesired.jpg).</div><div>I think that the ggplot attaches the exponent label like 10e3 instead of</div><div>10 x 10^3 because I rendered these graphs using another application.</div><div><br></div><div>My wish is to move this exponent label to the axis label.</div><div>It should appear as &quot;Left axis x 10^3&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>How can I work it around?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for your kind help.</div><div><br></div><div>Takayuki</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
